Beryllium: crash report functions for FreeBSD, which has no Crashpad

Purpose: the FreeBSD port removes crashpad.cc from the build (there is no
  Crashpad on FreeBSD) and fences Chromium's own calls into it with
  #if !BUILDFLAG(IS_BSD). Helium's crash reporting adds new calls
  (helium_crash_reporting.cc from helium/core/crash-reporting-prefs.patch,
  helium_crash_dialog_controller.cc from helium/ui/crash-dialog.patch) to
  four functions defined only in crashpad.cc: SetUploadConsentFromUser,
  GetReports, RequestSingleCrashUpload and DeleteCrashReport. The fifth
  Poudriere build (2 November 2026) compiled everything and then failed to
  link chrome with these four undefined symbols.
  This patch adds crashpad_bsd.cc, built on BSD in place of crashpad.cc,
  with definitions that state FreeBSD's real situation: there are never
  any crash reports and nothing is uploaded. The crash dialog therefore
  never appears, and no report can reach a crash server. One definition
  file instead of fencing Helium's nine call sites, so a Helium update that
  calls these functions again still links.
Stage: 4 (Beryllium series). Depends on the imported BSD patch
  patch-components_crash_core_app_BUILD.gn (stage 2) and on
  helium/core/crash-reporting-prefs.patch (stage 3), which declares
  SetUploadConsentFromUser and DeleteCrashReport.
Refreshed against: Chromium 156.0.8078.79, Helium 0.20.3 (2f81b9ca),
  FreeBSD ports 6ad3e0c8, using freebsd/tools/patch-workbench. Compiled
  against the post-stage-4 crashpad.h with FreeBSD's build_config.h and
  -Werror=missing-declarations, so every definition matches a declaration.
Known gap: Helium's crash reporting setting (Settings, Helium services)
  is still shown on FreeBSD and has no effect there.
Test: the build links chrome; functional (planned): no crash dialog after
  a forced renderer or browser crash; beryllium://crashes lists nothing.
security-review: not required (removes behaviour; no new input handling)

--- a/components/crash/core/app/BUILD.gn
+++ b/components/crash/core/app/BUILD.gn
@@ -106,6 +106,7 @@
 
   if (is_bsd) {
     sources -= [ "crashpad.cc" ]
+    sources += [ "crashpad_bsd.cc" ]
   }
 
   defines = [ "CRASH_IMPLEMENTATION" ]
--- /dev/null
+++ b/components/crash/core/app/crashpad_bsd.cc
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+// Copyright 2026 The Beryllium Authors
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
+
+// FreeBSD has no Crashpad: the FreeBSD port removes crashpad.cc from the
+// build. Helium's crash reporting settings and crash dialog call the report
+// functions below, so on FreeBSD they describe the true state: there are
+// never any crash reports, and nothing is ever uploaded.
+
+#include <string>
+#include <vector>
+
+#include "components/crash/core/app/crashpad.h"
+
+namespace crash_reporter {
+
+void SetUploadConsentFromUser(bool consent) {}
+
+void GetReports(std::vector<Report>* reports) {
+  reports->clear();
+}
+
+void RequestSingleCrashUpload(const std::string& local_id) {}
+
+bool DeleteCrashReport(const std::string& local_id) {
+  return false;
+}
+
+}  // namespace crash_reporter
